# Booking notification worker (Task 5)

This is a polling runtime for the existing PostgreSQL RPC contract. It does not use a broker.

Required environment:

- `SUPABASE_URL` (or `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_SUPABASE_URL`)
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`
- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_WORKER_ID` — explicit safe identity, unique per running instance

Optional:

- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_DRY_RUN=true` enables the non-delivery adapter for all channels. It is for contract tests/validation only.
- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_BATCH_SIZE` (default `25`, max `100`)
- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (default `5`, max `20`)
- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_BASE_RETRY_DELAY_MS` (default `30000`)
- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_MAX_RETRY_DELAY_MS` (default `3600000`)
- `BOOKING_NOTIFICATION_POLL_MS` (default `5000`)

Without dry-run, `whatsapp`, `telegram`, and `internal` are deliberately unconfigured and fail closed. No external delivery is claimed. A real provider must implement `NotificationAdapter` and be injected without changing the claim/complete flow.

Run from this directory with `bun test` or `bun run start`.
